  "hindi": "हे इन्द्र, दो हरे घोड़ों के साथ आ; चार के साथ आ; छह के साथ आ, बुलाया जाता हुआ; आठ और दस के साथ सोम पीने के लिए आ। यह निचोड़ा गया है, हे उदार; हानियाँ न कर।",
  "english": "Come, Indra, with two tawny horses; come with four; come with six, being called; come with eight and ten to the Soma-drink. This one is pressed, liberal one; do not make harm.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "The numerals qualify haribhiḥ (horses), taken from the first pāda; they have no noun of their own. The verb 'come' is repeated from yāhi. mā mṛdhaḥ kaḥ: 'do not make harm' is literal; mṛdh may mean 'harm, hostility, contempt' (uncertain), and its relation to the pressing is not stated. sumakha 'liberal' (makha: vigorous, bountiful; uncertain). 'This one' (ayam sutaḥ) is the pressed Soma, supplied from somapeyam.",
